---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro'

const bugReport = 'https://github.com/PaulWoitaschek/Voice/issues/new?template=bug.yml'
---

<Prose
  description="Check if your MP3 audiobook makes skips and resumes land in the wrong place, and fix it in your browser."
  title="MP3 books that jump"
>
  <h1>Does your MP3 book jump?</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    In some long MP3 audiobooks, a skip or a resume lands minutes away from the time Voice shows. Check your book here,
    and fix it if it's affected.
  </p>

  <div class="tool" data-state="idle">
    <label class="button primary pick">
      Choose an audiobook file
      <input accept=".mp3,audio/*" hidden type="file" />
    </label>
    <div class="checking">
      <p class="file"></p>
      <progress class="check-progress" max="1"></progress>
    </div>
    <div class="result">
      <p class="file"></p>
      <p data-verdict="other">
        This isn't an MP3 file, so it doesn't have this problem. If Voice still jumps in it,
        please <a href={bugReport}>report a bug</a>.
      </p>
      <p data-verdict="fine">
        This file is fine: a jump lands at most <span class="amount"></span> off. If Voice still jumps in it,
        please <a href={bugReport}>report a bug</a>.
      </p>
      <p data-verdict="broken">
        In this file, a jump can land up to <span class="amount"></span> away from where it should. Convert it to M4B to
        fix this, here or in one of the <a href="#fix">other ways</a>.
      </p>
      <button class="button primary convert" type="button">Convert to M4B</button>
      <button class="button tonal small again" type="button">Check another file</button>
    </div>
    <div class="working">
      <p class="file"></p>
      <progress class="convert-progress" max="1"></progress>
      <p class="muted status"></p>
      <button class="button tonal small cancel" type="button">Cancel</button>
    </div>
    <div class="done">
      <p class="file"></p>
      <p class="muted status"></p>
      <a class="button primary download">Download</a>
      <button class="button tonal small again" type="button">Check another file</button>
    </div>
    <p class="error" role="alert"></p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="why">Why MP3 books jump</h2>
  <p>
    Most audiobook MP3 files change their bitrate as they go. To find a time in such a file, a player has only a rough
    map with 100 points. In a book of 10 hours, that map can be off by minutes. M4B files have an exact map, so Voice can
    always go to the right place.
  </p>

  <h2 id="other-players">Why other players seem fine</h2>
  <p>
    Most players use the same rough map. In a test book, VLC started a minute early when it jumped to 5:30:00. You
    notice it more in Voice, because Voice jumps more often: it goes back a few seconds each time you pause, and it
    jumps to your place each time it loads the book. A player that plays from start to end never has to find a time.
  </p>

  <h2 id="fix">Ways to fix it</h2>
  <p>
    After each of them, put the new file in your audiobook folder and remove the old MP3 file, so Voice doesn't show the
    book twice.
  </p>

  <h3>In your browser</h3>
  <p>The converter above turns the book into an M4B file.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your book doesn't leave your device. Your browser does the conversion.</li>
    <li>The title, author, cover and chapters stay in the new file.</li>
    <li>The audio becomes AAC at 64 kbps, which is about 29 MB per hour.</li>
    <li>
      The whole book has to fit in memory. For very long books, use a computer, and keep the tab open until the download
      starts.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>With Audiobookshelf</h3>
  <p>
    If your books are on an Audiobookshelf server, edit the book, open <strong>Tools</strong>,
    and choose <strong>Make M4B Audiobook File</strong>.
  </p>

  <h3>With ffmpeg</h3>
  <p>On a computer with <a href="https://ffmpeg.org/download.html">ffmpeg</a>, this makes an M4B file with the chapters and the cover:</p>
  <pre><code>ffmpeg -i "book.mp3" -map 0:a -map "0:v?" -c:a aac -b:a 64k -c:v copy -disposition:v attached_pic "book.m4b"</code></pre>
  <p>
    To keep the MP3 audio as it is, split the book into 10 minute files instead. Voice plays all files in a folder as
    one book, but the chapter names are lost. Make the folder <code>book</code> first:
  </p>
  <pre><code>ffmpeg -i "book.mp3" -map 0:a -c copy -f segment -segment_time 600 -reset_timestamps 1 "book/part %03d.mp3"</code></pre>
</Prose>

<script>
  import { checkSeeking } from '../scripts/seek-check'

  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.tool')!
  const input = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input')!
  const checkProgress = root.querySelector<HTMLProgressElement>('.check-progress')!
  const convertProgress = root.querySelector<HTMLProgressElement>('.convert-progress')!
  const download = root.querySelector<HTMLAnchorElement>('.download')!
  const error = root.querySelector('.error')!
  let file: File | undefined
  let cancel: (() => Promise<void>) | undefined

  const show = (state: string, status = '') => {
    root.dataset.state = state
    root.querySelectorAll(`.${state} .status`).forEach((element) => (element.textContent = status))
  }

  const fail = (message: string, e: unknown) => {
    show('idle')
    error.textContent = message
    console.error(e)
  }

  input.addEventListener('change', async () => {
    file = input.files?.[0]
    if (!file) return
    input.value = ''
    root.querySelectorAll('.file').forEach((element) => (element.textContent = file!.name))
    error.textContent = ''
    show('checking')
    try {
      const result = await checkSeeking(file, (value) => (checkProgress.value = value))
      const verdict = result.kind === 'not-mp3' ? 'other' : result.errorSeconds < 5 ? 'fine' : 'broken'
      if (result.kind === 'mp3') {
        root.querySelectorAll('.amount').forEach((element) => (element.textContent = amount(result.errorSeconds)))
      }
      root.dataset.verdict = verdict
      show('result')
    } catch (e) {
      fail("This file couldn't be read.", e)
    }
  })

  root.querySelector('.convert')!.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    if (!file) return
    const name = file.name
    convertProgress.removeAttribute('value')
    show('working', 'Starting…')
    const started = performance.now()
    try {
      const { startConversion } = await import('../scripts/convert')
      const { conversion, result } = await startConversion(file, (value) => {
        convertProgress.value = value
        const left = value > 0.01 ? ((performance.now() - started) / value) * (1 - value) : NaN
        show('working', `${Math.floor(value * 100)} %` + (isNaN(left) ? '' : ` · about ${minutes(left)} left`))
      })
      cancel = () => conversion.cancel()
      const { blob, chapters } = await result
      URL.revokeObjectURL(download.href)
      download.href = URL.createObjectURL(blob)
      download.download = name.replace(/\.mp3$/i, '') + '.m4b'
      show('done', `${(blob.size / 1e6).toFixed(0)} MB, ${plural(chapters, 'chapter')}`)
    } catch (e) {
      if (root.dataset.state !== 'idle') fail("This file couldn't be converted.", e)
    } finally {
      cancel = undefined
    }
  })

  root.querySelector('.cancel')!.addEventListener('click', () => {
    show('idle')
    cancel?.()
  })

  root.querySelectorAll('.again').forEach((button) =>
    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      URL.revokeObjectURL(download.href)
      download.removeAttribute('href')
      file = undefined
      show('idle')
    }),
  )

  const plural = (value: number, word: string) => `${value} ${value === 1 ? word : `${word}s`}`
  const amount = (seconds: number) =>
    seconds < 90 ? plural(Math.max(1, Math.round(seconds)), 'second') : plural(Math.round(seconds / 60), 'minute')
  const minutes = (ms: number) => plural(Math.max(1, Math.round(ms / 60_000)), 'minute')
</script>

<style>
  .tool {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    justify-items: start;
    margin-block: 32px 48px;
    padding: clamp(20px, 4vw, 32px);
    border: 1px solid var(--card-line);
    border-radius: 28px;
    background: var(--card);
  }

  .tool p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pick,
  .tool button {
    border: 0;
    font-family: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .pick:focus-within {
    outline: 3px solid var(--primary);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .checking,
  .result,
  .working,
  .done {
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    justify-items: start;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .tool:not([data-state='idle']) .pick,
  .tool:not([data-state='checking']) .checking,
  .tool:not([data-state='result']) .result,
  .tool:not([data-state='working']) .working,
  .tool:not([data-state='done']) .done,
  .tool:not([data-verdict='other']) [data-verdict='other'],
  .tool:not([data-verdict='fine']) [data-verdict='fine'],
  .tool:not([data-verdict='broken']) :is([data-verdict='broken'], .convert) {
    display: none;
  }

  .file {
    font-weight: 600;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  progress {
    width: 100%;
    height: 8px;
    accent-color: var(--primary);
  }

  .error:empty {
    display: none;
  }

  .error {
    color: light-dark(#ba1a1a, #ffb4ab);
  }
</style>
